status  [green] Built 2 parts, RangeBox_r2_Layout, RangeBox_r2_Carrier_Carrier and RangeBox_r2.SLDASM, reusing the 4 parts already built; no interference between the gears in any mode, where they stand. Its turning gears are mated to turn in each of its 3 modes, one configuration each (H, N and L), and SolidWorks reports no mate in error in any of them: it opens in H; to switch mode, double-click another mode's configuration in SolidWorks' ConfigurationManager. Drag Sun in SolidWorks and the rest of its train follow. RangeSlv slides along Output, to its place in each mode. The 3 copies of Planet turn on Carrier, and RangeBox_r2_Carrier_Carrier holds Carrier's axes and planes only: a plate and pins are yours to add. Ring stays fixed where it is placed: its shaft does not turn. A turn you give the gears in one mode can show in other modes, so a dog can stand across its sleeve in another; to put the gears back there, press Update SolidWorks with that mode showing. 1 thing to do by hand: Assign a material to each of the 2 parts; the build leaves it unset. Carried into RangeBox_r2, unsaved: your Chain-1, Housing-1 (was Housing-2), Sprocket-1 and 14 other components, each where it stood. SolidWorks would not describe UserFaceConc wholly (its reference could not be read ('method' object is not iterable)), so it is not made again. SolidWorks would not describe UserFaceCoin wholly (its reference could not be read ('method' object is not iterable)), so it is not made again. SolidWorks would not describe UserSunFace wholly (its reference could not be read ('method' object is not iterable)), so it is not made again. SolidWorks would not describe UserAsm6 wholly, so it is not made again. SolidWorks would not describe UserAxis9 wholly, so it is not made again. UserGearRoot was on a face of Sun, and Sun's part is new because its Flank changed, so it is not made again. UserGearFillet was on a face of Sun, and Sun's part is new because its Flank changed, so it is not made again. Sol